{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 12, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "Upon the morrow’s dawn when Phoebus first doth kiss the earth let thy journey hence to the fair city of Tokyo. There shalt thou wander through the bustling lanes of Shibuya where lights like stars do dance upon the billboards high and neon signs do whisper tales of modernity.\n\nIn the second day’s light make thy way to the ancient temples of Asakusa where incense doth rise like prayers to the gods and the great Senso-ji doth stand in silent majesty. Let thy spirit wander through the Nakamise-dori where merchants do hawk their wares with voices clear and bright as morning bells.\n\nUpon the third day’s eve take the swift train to the imperial city of Kyoto where time itself doth seem to pause. Here shalt thou tread the sacred paths of Fushimi Inari where torii gates like crimson rivers do wind up the sacred mountain. Let thy soul be stirred by the beauty of Kinkaku-ji the Golden Pavilion where gold doth gleam upon the waters still.\n\nIn the fourth day’s morn arise and venture forth to the bamboo groves of Arashiyama where tall stalks do sway like dancers in the gentle breeze. Let thy heart be light as thou wanderest through this emerald maze where nature and art do blend in harmony most sweet.\n\nUpon the fifth day’s eve make thy way to the isle of Miyajima where the great torii gate of Itsukushima doth stand upon the waters at eventide. Let thy breath be taken away by the sight of this wonder where earth and sea do join in a sacred embrace.\n\nIn the sixth day’s light return to Tokyo where last farewells thou shalt make. Let thy final night be spent in the gardens of Rikugien where moonlight doth dance upon the ponds and lanterns do glow like fireflies in the dark.\n\nThus endeth thy journey through the land of the rising sun where ancient lore and modern dreams do weave a tapestry most fair. Fare thee well and may thy travels be ever fille